{Board No.4 was a Queen's Gambit, offered by W. M. Le Patourel (Oxford) and accepted by R. H. Prior (Cambridge). The game was quite even up to the twentieth move, when the Oxonian lost the exchange. At the call of time Mr Hoffer gave the game in favour of Black, in the following position, after Black's 30th move. (Source: The Field, 5 April 1890, p503)}  0-1

